{
  "$comment": "A worker unit whose media take carries SIDE outputs: a LIST of files on one pip (handles.outputs[].list) and a JSON (look) output beside the media (decided 2026-11-11). `unit` is derived from the fixture unit fixture-echo: its manifest with these outputs, this contract and this registry.outputType (units-manifest.test.mjs validates exactly that), its type and label renamed. Its first output `base` is the media take (an image); `layers` lists one run's images; `layerData` is JSON, one entry per layer in the same order. Both engines are held to every section. `jobs`: one finished job each — `outputData` is the job row's output_data; `nodeOutput` what the server's buildNodeOutputFromJobData makes of it (the media keys as for any media node, the list on the per-pip carrier `unitLists`, the JSON on `unitOutputs`; no `json`, which is a JSON-only unit's first output); `pips` what a plain (Selected) wire from each pip carries (the key \"\" is an edge naming no pip); `landing` the side fields every editor lane writes beside the media take, on the node and on the take (the canvas run's runProcessingNode over the job row, the server-run lanes over nodeOutput), `cleared` the side fields that patch empties — written as null, no value to every reader, so a saved take still says its run made none. A list output's `<id>NotSaved` (how many items its run made but could not store; 0 when it stored every one) rides beside it: on the node output as `unitListsNotSaved`, landed as `<id>NotSaved`. `saved`: a node's data — the editor's own reads of it and the server's seeded output (extractSavedNodeOutput) — where the media take's pip lists only the last batch of a run once per upstream item (`__listResults`), never the take history, and a side output reads the ACTIVE take's own field (a take carries the side fields it was made with; null is no value, never the node's) and the node's field when the take carries none. `lists`: what an Each wire from each pip fans out over (null: no fan-out), on both states. `collected` (where given): what a list operator (Filter List, no conditions) wired from each pip collects — a look pip its own JSON entries, never the take batch on `__listResults`. `defaults`: the mode an edge with no outputMode has, per pip (defaultEdgeOutputMode). `routes`: a wire from a pip into a legacy target lands EXACTLY what wires from Upload Image nodes holding `asUploads` would land there, in order (an image pip routes as an image source; a Bundle hands every item, each as its own image) — `iteration` is a fan-out row on an Each wire. `routes.bundleBranches`: a Bundle wire into a target that keeps its own Bundle branch ahead of the per-item routing (a carousel post: every item one media item; a fan-in input such as UGC Finish's clips: the whole list folded; a UGC node's handle: each item on that handle, as the editor's per-item wires land it) lands exactly `inputs` on both engines — never one image wire per item into the media routes. `batches`: the unit run once per upstream item (decided 2026-11-11, row-aligned) — `items` the upstream pictures, `rows` each run's job output_data in row order. `nodeOutput` is what the server's fan-out output (assembleFanOutResult) carries under those keys: the take pip's batch on `listResults`, each row's own side outputs on `listResultSideOutputs`, and on `unitLists` / `unitOutputs` / `unitListsNotSaved` EVERY row's — each list output's files row by row, the look output declared `alignedWith` that list its entries row by row, each entry carrying the row it came from (`row`, 0-based: its take's index in `listResults` / `__listResults`; a row that made none adds nothing, so it is a row index, never a position), the not-stored counts summed (@nodaro/render-rules unitBatchSideOutputs). Each layer-data entry also names the base its own run stored (`baseUrl`, that row's `imageUrl`): a layer is paired with its base by it, never by `row`, because a row whose run failed (`{ \"failed\": <error> }` in `rows`) leaves an empty take (\"\" on the live `listResults`, none on the saved one) and a wire from Base lists only the bases that were made — the third picture's base is Base's second item. In that case `collected` names the side pips only: a list operator on the server's LIVE lane collects the failed row's \"\" from the take pip, where the editor and the saved lanes skip it (a known difference; `selected.collected` holds the take pip on the lanes that agree). `data` is the node after the run as every editor lane lands it (the live server run, the load-time lanes, the canvas run once per item): its side fields hold every row's, each take its own row's untagged (a single run's layer data carries no `row`); it is also the saved state, read by `savedOutput` (extractSavedNodeOutput), `pips`, `lists`, `collected` and `routes` — the same on the live fan-out output. `shown` is what the node shows beside its active take (its own row's). `selected`: the same node with another take made active — Base reads that take, while Layers and Layer data still hand on every row's, as the take pip's Each wire lists the batch whichever take is active.",
